WispWasp source-code licensing status

No project-level open-source license has been declared for the WispWasp
project code in the upstream repository as of September 18, 2026.

Copyright in original project code remains with its respective author(s) and
contributors. Unless a particular file says otherwise, no permission is
granted by this repository to use, copy, modify, publish, distribute,
sublicense, or sell the project code beyond rights that already exist under
applicable law or the terms of the platform through which the repository is
made available.

The fact that the source repository is public, or that GitHub permits a
repository to be forked, is not by itself an open-source license.

Third-party software, libraries, tools, models, media, and other dependencies
retain their own licenses and are not covered by this notice. See
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

If the copyright holder(s) intend WispWasp to be open source, this file should
be replaced with the chosen license text only after the people who own the
relevant rights approve that license.
